7. SCRAP PRICING ENGINE
==================================================

Build a centralized dynamic scrap pricing engine.

Never hard-code actual scrap prices in the frontend.

Pricing must be configurable by:

- Material
- Category
- Grade
- City
- Zone
- Warehouse
- Unit
- Quantity
- Market rate
- Buying rate
- Selling rate
- Quality adjustment
- Collection cost
- Sorting cost
- Operational margin
- Effective date
- Expiry date

Example:

Market rate: Rs 180/kg
Quality adjustment: -Rs 10
Collection allocation: Rs 5
Operational margin: Rs 10

Illustrative customer buying price:

Rs 155/kg.

This is an example only. Admin must configure actual prices.

Pricing formula:

Customer Buying Price =
Approved Base Rate
+/- Quality Adjustment
- Allocated Collection Cost
- Operational Margin

For each pickup:

Total Amount =
Sum of Verified Material Weight × Approved Buying Rate.

Admin features:

- Create rates
